{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788281127,"nonce":"AG2v4wlWfc50oN5yWWN3+DoDq3g=","message":"ALL BULLETS PROVEN ON A LIVE BENCH — CLOSING. Session 16, 2026-09-01, assembly\n`479e4a1`. Record: `accept/runs/s16-20260901/`.\n\nThe two bullets left open by session 15's pass are now met.\n\n**1. The tolerated chair is LISTED.** Session B added `occupants` to an\nACCEPTED interaction row — additive, so `blocker` stays null and no existing\nfield changed meaning:\n\n    {\"at\": [140,140], \"role\": \"interaction\", \"ok\": true, \"reason\": null,\n     \"blocker\": null, \"standable\": true,\n     \"occupants\": [{\"def\": \"DiningChair\", \"label\": \"dining chair\",\n                    \"at\": [140,140], \"removal\": \"deconstruct\",\n                    \"tolerated\": true, ...}]}\n\nSo \"a chair is there, which is fine\" and \"the cell is empty\" no longer read\nalike — which matters because that chair is what the next bench's overlap check\ntrips on.\n\n**2. The survey's verdict and the build verb's refusal are the SAME SENTENCE.**\nSame arguments, same map, one routine:\n\n    site-survey -\u003e \"Interaction spot is blocked by pine tree.\"\n    build       -\u003e \"Interaction spot is blocked by pine tree.\"\n\n**3. The rotation search falls through, on ground where it is the only answer.**\nStaged the acceptance's own fixture — a corridor three cells wide between two\nwall runs — and asked for the 5x2 `HiTechResearchBench` with no `rot`:\n\n    at [171,171] 2x5 rot=West  pos=[172,173]\n    at [172,170] 2x5 rot=East  pos=[172,172]\n    at [172,169] 2x5 rot=East  pos=[172,171]\n    at [172,168] 2x5 rot=East  pos=[172,170]\n\nEvery candidate horizontal, and the refusals tally names the default first with\nthe game's own reason: `{pos:[172,173], rot:\"North\", footprint:{at:[170,173],\nw:5, h:2}, reason:\"Space already occupied.\"}`. A search that silently fixed\n`rot` would have reported \"no room\" for ground that has room.\n\nOne deviation from the bullet's text, stated rather than glossed: the same call\nwith `rot:\"North\"` pinned returned four candidates rather than none, because\nthe search radius reaches past the corridor onto open ground. The fixture, not\nthe verb, is what makes \"none\" achievable; the discriminating half — North\nrefused IN the corridor, East accepted there — is proven by the refusals tally\nabove.\n\n**4. The widget gate proven in BOTH directions on one map.** Before\n`dev:finish-research`, `find-rect {def:\"HiTechResearchBench\"}` refused without\nsearching at all — `examined: 0, gate_calls: 0`, `selectable: {ok:false,\nclause:\"research\", detail:\"needs research 'MicroelectronicsBasics'\"}`. After,\n`selectable: {ok:true, clause:null}` and the search ran. That is `1adc737`\namendment #1's god-hand closed, and closed through `WorldSafe.Finished`, so the\nsave was never polluted by the read.\n\nEverything from session 15's pass still stands: the exact corner↔centre\nround-trip, the even-axis rotation shift, the three tiers with `margin_facts`,\nboth interaction rules firing with the game's own strings, and `find-rect\n{w,h}` untouched (340 insertions, zero deletions).","files":null}]}